    <l n="1" para="true">@Gibolof, alias gittalof, superbit.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">@Gemacoda, Concinnabat] Affine</l>
    <l n="3">nostratium <i>to make</i>, à Sax. ȝemacian,</l>
    <l n="4">facere.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">@Ginroda, Genuit.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">@Geminsoda, Diminuit] Diminutio,</l>
    <l n="7">Saxonibus minyunȝ, nobis <i>mincing</i>:</l>
    <l n="8">ut cibus frustatim, &amp; minutim con-</l>
    <l n="9">cifus, nobis <i>mincedmeat</i>, alias <i>mincemeat</i>.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">@Segiroda, Paravit] Superiùs ad @Gi-</l>
    <l n="11">ʒo notatis, hîc adde, quòd vestimen-</l>
    <l n="12">tum, amictus, Saxonibus ȝyplan,</l>
    <l n="13">ȝeȝyplan; unde eis mnunc ȝeȝyplan,</l>
    <l n="14">pro habitu, sive apparatu monachico,</l>
    <l n="15">Bedæ, <i>Caracalla</i>: item vestimenta ec-</l>
    <l n="16">clesiastica, eis cyncean, ȝeȝynela;</l>
    <l n="17">@Geare, etiam in Scotorum @Gaoes</l>
    <l n="18">&amp; @Geare, pro bonis &amp; supelleƈtile,</l>
    <l n="19">quemadmodum in nostratium <i>nigbt-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>geare</i>, <i>bead-geare</i>, id est, nocturnali,</l>
    <l n="21">capitali, apparatu, huc, ni fallor, refe-</l>
    <l n="22">rendum.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">@Gimarsaba, Mirificavit. Vide</l>
    <l n="24">@Gomarda] Magnificare, Saxonibus mæp-</l>
    <l n="25">rian;</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">@Gssatundon, Acceleraverunt] Citò,</l>
    <l n="27">confestim, Sax. pona, nobis <i>soone</i>.</l>
